        "text": "shown in Figure 10-16.\nFrom here you should recognize the basic email interface features, such as the\nWrite button in the toolbar for creating a new message, or the Get Messages but-\nton for checking for new mail on the email server.\nFIGURE 10-16:\nThe main\nThunderbird mail\npage.\nFIGURE 10-15:\nThe Thunderbird\nmanual email\nserver dialog box.\nCHAPTER 10 Using the Internet 197\nAs with KMail, if you need to customize your ISP connections you need to do\nthat in the Account Settings page. Just click the menu button and choose\nPreferences \u00c1 Account Settings to open the Account Settings window, shown in\nFigure 10-17.\nFrom here you can select the Server Settings option on the left-hand side and fill\nout the additional information required to connect with your incoming ISP server,\nsuch as an encryption type.",
